            <h3>Strong Foundation</h3>
            <h4>Total Score: 58 / 60</h4>
            
            
        <p>
        Your responses show collective potential leadership thinking across multiple contexts. You focus on building others’ capabilities. You view leadership as developing people rather than controlling outcomes. Like Priya at her best, you measure true success by what others can accomplish on their own. 
        </p>
        <p><strong>Your strengths:</strong></p>
        <ul>
            <li>You focus on developing others’ capacity rather than solving problems for them </li>
            <li>You create systems and opportunities that help others succeed independently </li>
            <li>You measure success by what others accomplish rather than your personal achievements </li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>Growth opportunities:</strong></p>
        <ul>
            <li>Share your capacity-building approach to help other leaders avoid the competence paradox </li>
            <li>Look for mentoring opportunities to teach others about collective potential thinking</li>
            <li>Keep deepening your understanding of stewardship principles in complex leadership situations </li>
        </ul>
            
